WEBVTT

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone is about to start!

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.220
That's...

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.310
Tenma-kun! Greetings!

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.280
Perfect timing, Wondeba, as usual!

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.770
That's... Raimon's caravan?

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.590
The first half ends here!

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.200
A predetermined recess.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.570
What an annoying rule.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.380
Woop.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:22.130
Fei, are events panning out?

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.100
Things got a little rough.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:31.190
As I thought, you won't get far without me, Clark Wonderbat-sama, the greatest coach of all time!

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:32.910
Coach?

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:33.980
But you're a bear!

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.790
And a stuffed toy!

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.450
They disappeared!

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.120
I didn't mention, but they're a type of Avatar that I create.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.150
They're called Dupli and they act as player stand-ins.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.690
They don't have any substance.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:50.130
So... they don't really exist?

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.910
Tenma-kun, don't worry.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:57.340
I've restored your timeline where you first encounter soccer.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.840
I see.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.620
It takes time before a timeline that's been modified becomes fixed.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:07.060
The closer you are to the event after it's been changed, the easier it is to change it back.

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:10.710
Oh, and did you get what I asked for?

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:11.950
Of course!

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.390
There's nothing Wondeba-sama can't do!

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:16.150
Really?! Wow!

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.390
Show me!

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.580
No need to rush!

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:23.580
But it did almost cost me my life, so you'd better be grateful!

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:24.830
Okay!

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:25.510
Let's go!

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.680
That's... a dinosaur?!

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:41.930
It's the Tyrannosaurus Rex!

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:43.370
C'mon, Fei!

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:44.550
Mixi-max!

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:46.130
Okay!

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:53.860
What's happening?

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.820
Fei, are you okay?

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:09.660
Yeah.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:13.580
This is Mixi-max!

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:19.590
The Mixi-max gun combines both my personality and the T-Rex's personality together.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:20.970
That's why I look like this.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.740
I-I see...

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:23.510
That's that.

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:27.160
I think it's time we squared this match away... {そろそろ試合を四万十川 idk how to translate this one. if he makes any more puns i'm gonna kill him xD}

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.330
Then let the second half begin!

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:37.330
Fei!

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:48.310
Incredible... he's even better than before!

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:50.290
Tenma!

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:51.450
M-Me?!

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.270
Their dimension is just too different!

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:56.050
You'll be fine!

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.280
I'm telling you, your eyes just aren't used to it!

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.710
Calm down and focus!

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.750
That's right, concentrate!

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.720
Things will work out somehow!

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:12.050
Oh dear, the ball gets stolen from Matsukaze in the blink of an eye!

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:15.680
Is it impossible for him to catch up with Protocol Omega?

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:23.080
Wonder Trap!

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:25.730
I saw it!

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.240
You won't get through!

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:33.170
Aggressive Beat!

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.980
Matsukaze suddenly lets off a chain of hissatsu techniques!

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:43.020
I did it!

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:44.880
You're awesome, Tenma!

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:45.250
Thanks!

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.240
So it's true.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.750
Matsukaze Tenma is...

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.600
Ancient Fangs!

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.960
Keeper Command 03!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.580
<Boom Shout>

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:10.740
It's in!

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.140
Tenmas bring it up to a tie!

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:14.410
Yes!

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:15.430
He's...

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:16.450
We're tied!

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.910
Ruler of the Skies,

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:25.980
Phoenix!

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:28.630
Armed!

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:42.450
He's coming!

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:46.020
Hissatsu tactics, AX3!

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:47.430
<Bermuda Wave>

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:53.270
Tenmas' movements have gotten slower!

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:54.920
I can't move...

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:04.470
Protocol Omega cuts through Tenmas!

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.280
Are you okay?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:10.160
Holding up nine Dupli consumes a lot of my aura...

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.810
But there's no other way.

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:13.640
Fei...

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:18.000
Fei!

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:24.140
Whoa!

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:29.950
This is Alpha.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:33.070
Is that true?

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:41.270
Someone has remodified the Interruption point for Matsukaze Tenma over our own modification.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:44.320
Modification has occurred twice.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:47.650
This now makes it harder for us to change history.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:53.300
Because of it, the flow of time will spontaneously repair itself in order to conserve its original timeline.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:56.140
The situation has grown troublesome.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:58.160
You must temporarily abort this mission.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:07:59.470
Yes.

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:01.370
As you ordered.

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:05.010
What happened, sir?

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:08.990
Our modification of the Interruption point earlier has been rendered invalid.

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:11.670
Who could do such a thing?

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.590
It must have been them.

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:15.700
What's going on, Alpha?

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:17.880
This match is cancelled.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:19.400
Hey, wait...!

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:21.590
Fei, is this...?

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:25.600
So, since you forfeit, that means we win this one.

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:39.320
Fei, tell me.

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:41.100
What's happening right now?

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:43.560
What happened to the soccer club? To soccer?

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:45.050
Fei!

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:50.670
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:55.690
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:02.120
We came from 200 years into the future.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:02.850
The future?

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:04.040
Yep.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.020
We're here to stop those who are trying to erase soccer.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:09.580
Do you know what parallel worlds are?

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:11.270
Parallel worlds?

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:12.310
Look at this.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:21.910
When a certain point on a timeline is changed, it can create alternate paths in reality.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.420
Those are parallel worlds.

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:30.900
By traveling through time and changing the most important events that involve Raimon's soccer club,

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:35.100
they've created a world where Raimon doesn't have a soccer club.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:36.300
In other words...

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.910
Raimon's soccer club got erased...

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:40.800
That's not all.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:44.130
Their main objective is to erase soccer itself.

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:46.030
Erase it? Why?!

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:50.960
Having soccer exist is an inconvenience to them.

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:53.150
Who's "them"?

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:56.400
An organization that acts as decision-makers for the entire world.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:57.660
El Dorado.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.300
My apologies, Chairman.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.510
Failure is inexcusable.

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:07.090
You must eliminate soccer, or the world could be destroyed.

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:08.400
You do understand this?

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:12.050
The world is currently at war.

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:16.680
The enemy are children who are meant to be feared, Second Stage Children.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:21.650
They view us as inferior beings and attempt to control us.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:25.950
Their organization, Feida, are now a menace to mankind. {ﾌｪｰﾀﾞ}

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:30.880
We must take quick action and eliminate them.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:35.670
Their genes come from talented soccer players.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:37.670
Soccer has created them.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:44.670
Therefore, we must prevent soccer from expanding and stop mankind from evolving down the wrong path.

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:46.390
Do you understand?

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:48.440
All of it, sir.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:53.670
Then don't disappoint us, Alpha.{isn't alpha a SSC too?!?}

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:55.820
Yes, master.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:00.910
I can't believe that's what's happening in the future...

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:04.730
El Dorado fears Second Stage Children.

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:10.100
That's why they intend to erase soccer and prevent them from being born into the world.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:12.020
Erase soccer...

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:15.510
No one has the right to do that, no matter what the reason is!

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:17.260
Exactly.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:20.250
But that sort of reasoning won't work on El Dorado.

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:23.870
But those guys were playing soccer, too.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:25.280
So why...?

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.230
Because it's the most effective way.

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:33.810
When soccer players are beaten by soccer that's on the same stage as theirs, it causes the greatest emotional damage.

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:36.790
That makes it easier to change their feelings towards soccer.

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:38.060
No way!

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:40.300
Soccer is meant to be fun...

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:44.070
Yes. Soccer is meant to be fun...

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:45.840
And for some people, it's necessary.

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:50.240
That's why we're here.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:51.870
To save you.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:54.040
Fei, why are you doing this?

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:58.760
There are still people in the future who love soccer just like you, Tenma.

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:01.620
I'm one of those who needs soccer.

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:02.830
Fei...

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.910
That's why I'll protect soccer along with you.

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:09.400
Thanks, Fei!

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:10.670
Let's go, Tenma.

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:12.190
Go? Where?

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:15.600
First, we need to take back Raimon's soccer club.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:19.870
To do that, we need to go to the place where Raimon's soccer was born.

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:25.600
To Raimon Junior High eleven years ago, on the day Endou Mamoru made the Raimon soccer club.

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:28.110
You mean we'll be time traveling?

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:28.960
Yep.

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:35.790
The reason why Raimon's soccer club disappeared is because the historical Interruption point when it was first made got modified.

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:37.100
Interruption point?

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:43.250
An Interruption point is like a fateful turning point that can change history.

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:47.480
They intervene at those points and remake what occurs there.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.980
So that's what happened to Raimon's soccer club...

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:53.910
Yeah. And it's our job to change them back to normal.

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:56.800
Okay.

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:01.590
Okay! Then, if we're finished talking...

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:05.450
This is a time machine?

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:06.290
Yep.

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:09.270
Or to be more precise, a space-time transportation device.

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:13.680
It can slip through wormholes to different times and places.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:18.740
I made it and based its exterior on the caravan that you have for Raimon's soccer club.

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:21.400
So we use this to go to different times?

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:24.310
Yeah, but there is a requirement we need to fulfill first.

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:28.240
If we want to time jump to a specific time, we need a guide.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:29.230
A guide?

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:32.560
We call them Artifacts.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:37.630
It has to be an object that is filled with the strong feelings of someone from that time and place.

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:42.730
Without it, we won't be able to detect the right exit in the wormhole and the time jump will fail.

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:46.870
Then what do we need to go back eleven years?

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:50.470
Something that is filled with feelings when the soccer club was first made.

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:52.930
Tenma, got any ideas?

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:57.540
I know! The soccer club's old clubroom!

00:13:57.540 --> 00:14:01.130
That's where Coach Endou made the soccer club for the first time.

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:02.910
Maybe it has something!

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:17.900
Huh? It looks different from what I remember...

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:23.390
Looks more like they used it for storage than a clubroom.

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:29.150
Coach Endou said that this place was here way before he even came to this school.

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:31.550
So there must be something in here!

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:36.340
Are you sure it's in here?

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:38.080
Wait a sec! Look...

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:42.270
All right! This is it!

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:48.120
Artifact set.

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:53.880
I hope it works...

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:55.880
"Things will work out", remember?

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:57.020
Right.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:58.750
Then let's go!

00:15:02.930 --> 00:15:05.020
Wormhole cycle confirmed!

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:06.650
Beginning time route detection!

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:08.110
Collating coordinate axes!

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:09.950
T minus 5 seconds to time jump!

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:10.980
4...

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:11.950
3...

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:13.070
2...

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:14.210
1...

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:16.170
Time jump!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.810
This is...

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:36.030
It should be the day that Endou Mamoru starts his first day at Raimon.

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:38.030
What beautiful cherry blossoms.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:43.710
There's Coach Endou!

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:48.290
No, he's neither Coach nor Captain right now.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:51.990
He isn't even in the soccer club yet.

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:54.750
A Coach Endou who isn't in the soccer club, huh...

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.720
I'm here at last!

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:03.050
What's the matter, Tenma?

00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:07.330
Coach Endou will be making Raimon's soccer club starting today, right?

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:10.290
Yeah. If nothing goes wrong.

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:14.520
I want to join the soccer club!

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:18.630
Sorry, but our school doesn't have a soccer club.

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.680
Don't react to everything!

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:25.290
Sorry, I got caught up in the moment...

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:37.490
This is how Raimon's history begins.

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:38.450
Yeah.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:42.760
What's that?

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:45.580
Hey, isn't that...

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:48.450
I thought so!

00:16:48.710 --> 00:16:50.360
The clubroom's doorplate!

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:55.870
All right!

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:57.350
Raimon's soccer club is now...

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:58.750
Ready for business!

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:04.790
I hope the soccer club works out.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:07.950
Yeah. You're going to build up the soccer club, right, Endou-kun?

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:10.860
Yeah, I'll make it survive no matter what!

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:13.420
I know you can do it.

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:16.120
Really? You think so?

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:19.880
Aki-nee and Coach Endou look so young!

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:22.590
Tenma-kun, are those two dating?

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:25.590
Wondeba, don't be indelicate.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:30.040
There's so much I want to do when we get the soccer club going.

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:32.630
There's this competition called Football Frontier-

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:33.870
Give it up.

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:39.330
Raimon cannot make a soccer club.

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:41.770
Are they your friends, Kino?

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:43.330
I don't know them.

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:46.820
You cannot make a soccer club. This is a fact.

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:49.260
What gives you the right to decide that?

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:50.570
You don't know for certain!

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:55.470
We can make a soccer club, so long as people who really like soccer join up!

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:58.130
No one likes soccer.

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:00.410
No one?

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:01.540
What are you talking about?

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:04.490
There's someone who does like soccer.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.260
Right here.

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:07.410
Endou-kun...

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:09.900
You will grow to hate it soon enough.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:13.020
I will never hate soccer.

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:14.280
I see.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:16.260
Move Mode.

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:21.480
Oh no!

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:22.400
Let's go, too!

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:31.310
Where are we?

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:34.520
It's the perfect place to steal soccer from you.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:36.650
Fei, where is this?

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:38.990
Football Frontier Stadium.

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:42.930
Historically, it's where Endou Mamoru fought to win best in Japan.

00:18:43.340 --> 00:18:44.360
Here...

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:46.590
What's going on here?

00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:51.370
You will now be playing soccer against us in a match.

00:18:52.210 --> 00:18:53.450
A match?

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:54.560
What do you mean?

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:56.430
Coach Endou!

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.800
I mean, Endou-san!

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:01.510
These guys are trying to erase soccer.

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:04.220
Um, and you are...?

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:06.800
Oh, uh, I'm Matsukaze Tenma.

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:10.080
Er, um... there's too much to explain, but...

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:13.920
I came here to protect the soccer that I love.

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:16.610
If we don't do something right now, things will get really bad!

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:17.660
You have to believe me!

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:20.970
Okay.

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:23.430
You believe me?

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:24.500
Yeah.

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:27.950
Since you say you love soccer, I believe you.

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:30.430
You can't lie about what you love, after all.

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:33.340
What you just said is true, right?

00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:34.600
That's right.

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:35.900
Then I'll play your match.

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:36.660
Bring it on!

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:40.630
Then I'll teach you guys how much fun soccer can be.

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:44.330
But you have eleven players on your team already.

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:45.910
That's a problem, we're...

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.210
Don't worry, we're good.

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:50.800
They're all friends who love soccer too.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:52.610
Who are they?

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:56.280
I received information.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:20:00.330
They have traveled through time to nullify our modifications.

00:20:01.060 --> 00:20:05.710
It seems they have already fought with us in another parallel world.

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:06.770
I see.

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:07.950
What do we do, sir?

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:10.650
Endou Mamoru and Matsukaze Tenma.

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:14.100
We just have to take soccer from the both of them at once.

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:18.600
Honey, we're ready to open shop.

00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:20.340
Yeah, go ahead!

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:26.830
Huh?

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:29.330
He slipped out again?

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:33.330
Why am I holding a mic?

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:39.130
I thought I was in the kitchen, but now I'm on soccer grounds in who-knows-where?!

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:41.390
See to it.

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:46.840
Now, the match between Tenmas and Protocol Omega begins anew!

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:49.290
Okay, everyone!

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:51.290
Let's play soccer!

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:55.690
What?

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.500
How horrible...

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:12.640
They know that the Dupli are controlled remotely, so they're blocking Fei's field of vision while hurting the Dupli.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:16.510
Wait!

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.560
Soccer...

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:20.400
Soccer isn't meant to be used like this!

00:22:54.650 --> 00:22:55.960
Standing on the same field as him is like a dream!

00:22:55.960 --> 00:23:00.180
I'll protect soccer with Coach Endou from eleven years ago!

00:23:00.500 --> 00:23:02.910
Next, Revive! Raimon!!

00:23:03.210 --> 00:23:05.150
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.170 --> 00:23:19.070
The Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone's proverb today is...

00:23:23.370 --> 00:23:26.700
You can't lie about what you love!

00:23:26.700 --> 00:23:27.390
That's all!
